esn't create a Tile Hog issue.\n- **Play T8**: T8 has two unseen copies. No other player has shown interest in high Bamboos, and T7-T9 are partially depleted. Could be safe, but T8 might help complete chows like 6-7-8 or 7-8-9. Next player discarded T7 recently\u2014possible danger.\n- **Play W9**: W9 has two unseen copies. High Characters are somewhat open; next player played W8 and W7, suggesting they may be discarding them. Also, I have no use for W9 in any sequence (my W-chow is 2-3-4). Holding onto it offers little benefit.\n\nReason: Among all options, **F2** stands out because it matches both seat and prevalent wind. While discarding it gives information, **keeping it preserves the chance to form a valuable pung later**, especially since two F2s remain unclaimed. In contrast, **W9 has no strategic future in my hand**, doesn\u2019t contribute to any possible chow or pung, and isn\u2019t involved in knitted patterns. Other players aren\u2019t showing W9 interest, and W7-W8-W9 sequences seem unlikely given prior discards. Thus, W9 is the safest and most expendable tile.\n\nAnswer: Play W9"}
