 B6 tiles have not been seen \u2014 but I see one in my hand, one in previous player's meld \u2192 so two visible \u2192 two unvisible \u2192 should be 2.\n\nBut listed as 3 \u2014 inconsistency.\n\nPerhaps the number is **count of remaining tiles**, not unshown.\n\nRe-read: \"Unshown tiles are: [W1: 1; ... B6: 3]\"\n\nGiven that, and knowing standard rules, assume it means **number of tiles of that type still available in wall or opponents' hands**, i.e., **not yet discarded or melded publicly**.\n\nBut my melds and hand are private \u2014 so when counting unshown, it excludes what I hold.\n\nAh! Critical: **\"Unshown tiles\" likely means tiles not revealed to you**, i.e., excluding your own hand and public melds.\n\nSo:\n- Total B6: 4\n- Publicly used: previous player has [B6,B7,B8] \u2192 1 B6 exposed\n- Discarded: check histories \u2014 no B6 discarded\n- My hand: 1 B6 \u2014 but this is not \"shown\" to others, so included in \"unshown\"?\nBut the list is presented to me \u2014 so probably \"unshown\" means **not visible to anyone**, i.e., remaining in wall or hidden in hands.\n\nBut the number includes my hand?\n\nFor example, I have W3 \u2014 unshown says W3:1 \u2014 and I have one W3 \u2014 so likely \"unshown\" means **total remaining tiles not yet drawn or discarded**, i.e., **available in game**.\n\nSo W3:1 \u2192 only one W3 left anywhere \u2014 I have it in hand.\n\nThen when I discard it, it becomes zero.\n\nSimilarly, B6:3 \u2192 three B6 tiles still exist somewhere \u2014 but I have one, previous player used one \u2192 two accounted \u2192 implies two more? Impossible.\n\nUnless the meld uses more than one.\n\nNo \u2014 [B6,B7,B8] uses one B6.\n\nTotal: 4 copies.\n\nIf B6:3 unshown \u2192 3 remain \u2192 only one used \u2192 but previous player used one, so ok only if no other used.\n\nBut I have one in hand \u2014 is that counted?\n\nYes \u2014 \"unshown\" probably means **not revealed on table**, so includes hidden tiles in all hands and wall.\n\nSo B6:3 \u2192 total of 3 B6 tiles are still in play (in hands or wall), including mine.\n\nSo one B6 has been discarded or used in exposed meld.\n\nPrevious player has [B6,B7,B8] \u2192 exposed one B6.\n\nSo total B6: 4 \u2192 1 exposed \u2192 3 unshown (in hands/wall) \u2192 matches.\n\nSimilarly, I have one B6 in hand \u2192 part of the 3.\n\nSo remaining B6 tiles not in my hand: 2.\n\nSame for others.\n\nSo correction:\n- For any tile, \"unshown: N\" means N copies are still in play (not discarded or exposed).\n- This includes my hand and others' hands and wall.\n\nSo for B6: 3 unshown \u2192 3 copies still in circulation \u2192 I have one \u2192 2 others out there.\n\nSimilarly:\n- T8: 2 unshown \u2192 I have one \u2192 1 other\n- F2: 2 unshown \u2192 I have one \u2192 1 other\n- W3: 1 unshown \u2192 I have one \u2192 0 others\n- B3: 2 unshown \u2192 I have one, and my meld [B3,B4,B5] has one \u2192 2 used \u2192 2 unshown \u2192 so 2 others out there? No:\n  - Total B3: 4\n  - Used in my meld: 1\n  - In my hand: 1\n  - So 2 accounted\n  - Thus 2 unshown \u2192 yes, matches\n  - So 2 B3 tiles still available (in wall or others' hands)\n\nAh! So \"unshown\" includes all non-exposed tiles.\n\nSo re-evaluate availability:\n\n- W3: 1 unshown \u2192 only one exists \u2192 I have it \u2192 **no more W3 available**\n- Therefore, **cannot draw another W3** \u2192 W3 cannot become a pair\n- Similarly, T8: 2 unshown \u2192 I have 1 \u2192 1 more exists\n- F2: 2 unshown \u2192 I have 1 \u2192 1 more exists\n- B3: 2 unshown \u2192 I have 1 \u2192 1 more exists (plus one in my meld)\n- B6: 3 unshown \u2192 I have 1 \u2192 2 more exist\n\nSo:\n- W3: **only one in existence, I have it** \u2192 **cannot pair** \u2192 **useless for pairing**\n- Therefore, **must discard W3** \u2014 it offers zero chance to form a pair\n- All others have at least one more copy\n\nThus, **Play W3** is the only logical choice \u2014 it's a dead tile.\n\nKeeping W3 guarantees I cannot pair it. I must rely on drawing a duplicate of another tile, but W3 is gone forever.\n\nWhereas:\n- T8: one more out there\n- F2: one more\n- B3: one more (since two unshown, I have one, so one other)\n- B6: two others\n\nSo only W3 is completely unavailable for pairing.\n\nTherefore, discard W3.\n\nThen my hand becomes: T8, B3, B6, F2 \u2014 all of which have at least one more copy \u2014 so I can potentially pair any of them.\n\nNext draw, if I get another T8, F2, etc., I can win.\n\nAlso, no one is showing interest in W3 \u2014 not worth holding.\n\nEvaluation:\n- Play W3: eliminates a dead tile, keeps only live ones \u2014 best.\n- Play B6: keeps W3 (dead), worse.\n- Play T8: T8 has a chance, W3 does not \u2014 worse.\n- Play F2: same, F2 has a chance, W3 does not.\n- Play B3: same.\n\nOnly **Play W3** removes a tile with zero chance of forming a pair.\n\nReason: W3 has only one copy in the entire game (as per unshown count of 1, and I hold it), so no duplicate exists to complete a pair. Keeping it makes it impossible to form a pair from it. Discarding it allows me to focus on pairing T8, B3, B6, or F2, all of which have additional copies available.\n\nAnswer: Play W3"}
